WEBVTT

00:04.500 --> 00:07.778
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.846 --> 00:11.023
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.091 --> 00:14.035
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.102 --> 00:17.913
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.980 --> 00:21.024
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.091 --> 00:22.637
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.705 --> 00:23.986
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.054 --> 00:26.318
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.669 --> 00:36.683
ANNOUNCER (on TV):
And now our feature
presentation,

00:36.752 --> 00:39.273
<i>Lawrence of Arabia,
presented in its original</i>

00:39.341 --> 00:41.692
Ulta-Cinemascope
letterbox format.

00:41.761 --> 00:44.112
(music theme plays)

00:44.180 --> 00:45.756
LOIS:
Well, I can't see anything.

00:45.823 --> 00:48.072
STEWIE:
Who's the rather attractive
girl on the camel?

00:48.140 --> 00:49.313
BRIAN:
That's Peter O'Toole.

00:49.381 --> 00:50.925
PETER:
You film buffs might enjoy this.

00:50.993 --> 00:54.377
Both his first and last names
are slang for "penis."

00:54.445 --> 00:57.096
We interrupt this program
to bring you exciting news.

00:57.163 --> 00:59.512
<i>Family Feud
will be coming to Quahog.</i>

00:59.579 --> 01:02.232
Auditions are being held
tomorrow at the Civic Center.

01:02.301 --> 01:04.314
<i>Family Feud's
coming to Quahog?</i>

01:04.382 --> 01:05.687
Peter, we
should try out.

01:05.756 --> 01:08.474
A family can win
$5,000 on that show.

01:08.541 --> 01:10.353
$5,000?

01:10.421 --> 01:12.734
I could get that cave for the
front yard I've always wanted,

01:12.802 --> 01:14.513
and then tell people
not to go in there.

01:14.581 --> 01:16.693
(kids laughing)

01:16.762 --> 01:18.304
Hey, you kids stay
out of that cave!

01:18.372 --> 01:20.550
You don't know
what's in there!

01:20.617 --> 01:23.333
(sighs)
Money well spent.

01:27.655 --> 01:29.929
We're looking for fun,
interesting families

01:29.997 --> 01:31.468
that viewers will
want to watch.

01:31.536 --> 01:33.173
You folks have any
interesting stories?

01:33.241 --> 01:34.779
Lois, tell him about
the whole stitches thing

01:34.847 --> 01:36.548
when Chris was born.
Never mind, I'll tell it.

01:36.616 --> 01:38.992
Lois was so wrecked,
they had to sew her up

01:39.060 --> 01:41.304
and open up a new vagina
right next to the first one.

01:41.372 --> 01:43.045
You know, kinda like
when they build a new bridge

01:43.114 --> 01:44.254
next to the old bridge,
and you're like,

01:44.321 --> 01:46.363
"Wow, I can't believe
I used to use the old one.

01:46.431 --> 01:47.635
Looks so unsafe."

01:47.703 --> 01:48.841
All right, enough
clowning around.

01:48.909 --> 01:49.946
<i>Let's talk turkey.
We want to play the Feud.</i>

01:50.014 --> 01:51.322
Well, you're in luck.

01:51.389 --> 01:53.532
The other family we've chosen
has three daughters,

01:53.599 --> 01:56.678
so we're picking you
because you have three sons.

01:56.746 --> 01:59.090
<i>But I'm not...
Shut up, Greg.</i>

01:59.158 --> 02:01.770
<i>(Family Feud theme song
playing)</i>

02:01.838 --> 02:06.022
<i>ANNOUNCER:
It's time for the Family Feud.</i>

02:06.090 --> 02:08.602
Introducing
the Callaghan Family.

02:08.670 --> 02:11.313
Ready for action.

02:11.380 --> 02:13.824
And the Griffin Family.

02:13.892 --> 02:17.342
On your marks, let's start...

02:17.410 --> 02:20.423
<i>the Family Feud!</i>

02:20.491 --> 02:22.432
<i>With the star of Family Feud...</i>

02:22.500 --> 02:24.441
Richard Dawson!

02:24.509 --> 02:26.450
Thank you. Thank you very much.

02:26.518 --> 02:27.789
Ah, you're lovely.

02:27.857 --> 02:29.195
I haven't heard
that much applause

02:29.263 --> 02:31.873
since Bob Crane premiered
his home movies in my closet.

02:31.941 --> 02:32.912
(Peter laughs)

02:32.980 --> 02:34.352
<i>All right, let's play the Feud.</i>

02:34.420 --> 02:36.997
♪ ♪
(applause)

02:37.065 --> 02:39.577
100 people surveyed,
top four answers on the board.

02:39.644 --> 02:40.817
Here's the question:

02:40.885 --> 02:43.161
Name something you find
in your bathroom.

02:43.228 --> 02:44.199
(buzzer)

02:44.268 --> 02:45.204
A sink.

02:45.273 --> 02:46.511
Show us "sink!"

02:46.579 --> 02:47.919
(bell rings)

02:49.492 --> 02:51.665
Peter, three answers
on the board that can beat that.

02:51.733 --> 02:54.609
Name something you find
in your bathroom.

02:54.676 --> 02:57.622
Find in your bathroom.
Find in your bathroom.

02:57.690 --> 03:00.267
Richard, I'm going to go
with "fetus in the toilet bowl."

03:00.334 --> 03:02.309
Show us "fetus
in the toilet bowl!"

03:02.376 --> 03:04.418
(bell rings, applause)

03:04.485 --> 03:06.458
Play or pass?
We're going to play.

03:06.526 --> 03:09.906
Oh, this must be
your lovely wife.

03:10.946 --> 03:12.887
(chuckling):
Oh, uh-uh.

03:12.955 --> 03:15.564
I've been waiting
for this for years.

03:15.632 --> 03:18.209
(moaning)

03:24.973 --> 03:28.420
Okay, Lois, name something
you find in your bathroom.

03:28.489 --> 03:30.597
Okay, how about
"bathtub?"

03:30.665 --> 03:31.971
(bell rings)

03:32.038 --> 03:34.514
(all cheering)

03:34.582 --> 03:37.525
Okay, name something you find
in your bathroom.

03:37.593 --> 03:39.165
Um...

03:39.233 --> 03:41.207
a razor blade
and a note?

03:41.276 --> 03:42.915
(bell rings)

03:42.984 --> 03:45.761
(all cheering)

03:45.829 --> 03:48.807
♪ ♪

03:52.491 --> 03:55.569
Name something you'd like
to receive as a gift.

03:55.637 --> 03:56.909
Candy?

03:56.976 --> 03:58.114
Show me "candy!"

03:58.182 --> 03:59.655
(buzzer)

03:59.722 --> 04:00.859
(audience sighs)

04:00.927 --> 04:02.266
Wait. We're out?

04:02.334 --> 04:04.275
But you said if I slept
with you...
All right, Griffins,

04:04.343 --> 04:05.948
here's your chance
to win the game!

04:06.016 --> 04:08.961
Name something you'd like
to receive as a gift.

04:09.030 --> 04:10.533
Groceries!
Assorted lotions!

04:10.601 --> 04:12.474
An Uzi!
A dead squirrel!
Money!

04:12.542 --> 04:13.980
All right, good answer,
good answer!
Yeah, money!

04:14.047 --> 04:15.552
Oh, very good!
Good answer!
There you go!
There you go!

04:15.619 --> 04:17.725
Well, Richard, my family seems
to think money's the way to go.

04:17.794 --> 04:19.231
So I'm gonna go
with the flute

04:19.300 --> 04:22.074
that Captain Picard played,
first in his imagination

04:22.142 --> 04:24.417
and then in real life, in the
episode "The Inner Light"

04:24.485 --> 04:26.090
<i>from Star Trek:
The Next Generation.</i>

04:26.158 --> 04:28.698
What?! No, you idiot!
We said "money!"

04:28.767 --> 04:30.305
Show me "Picard's flute!"

04:30.373 --> 04:31.641
(bell rings)

04:31.709 --> 04:34.786
(all cheering)

04:34.854 --> 04:36.794
Peter, how did you...?
I was in the survey.

04:36.861 --> 04:39.000
Can you believe it?
We're going to the bonus round!

04:39.069 --> 04:40.540
♪ ♪

04:40.607 --> 04:42.012
(applause)

04:42.080 --> 04:44.020
Okay, Lois.
15 seconds on the clock.

04:44.088 --> 04:45.692
Name something
you sit in.

04:45.761 --> 04:47.132
A chair.
My own feces.

04:47.200 --> 04:48.470
Name a popular fruit.

04:48.538 --> 04:49.741
Orange.
Clay Aiken.

04:49.810 --> 04:51.080
Something in your closet.

04:51.148 --> 04:52.418
Shoes.
Scary monsters.

04:52.486 --> 04:53.623
Your favorite holiday.

04:53.691 --> 04:54.895
Christmas.
9/11.

04:54.962 --> 04:56.734
Something you do
on the weekends.

04:56.803 --> 04:58.608
Go to church.
Black guys.

04:58.676 --> 05:00.013
(bell rings, applause)

05:00.081 --> 05:02.187
All right,
"Something you sit in."

05:02.256 --> 05:03.525
You said "chair."

05:03.593 --> 05:04.729
Survey said...

05:04.798 --> 05:06.034
(bell rings)

05:06.101 --> 05:07.539
Wait a sec. I said "feces."

05:07.608 --> 05:08.910
Where's my answer?

05:08.978 --> 05:10.751
Oh, you're just going to pretend
I'm not here, huh?

05:10.818 --> 05:13.762
Just like Robin Williams' agent
pretends he's still funny.

05:13.829 --> 05:15.601
(rings)
Hello?

05:15.669 --> 05:17.275
Hey, Phil, it's
Robin Williams.

05:17.343 --> 05:19.616
(laughs)
That's hilarious!

05:19.684 --> 05:22.293
I just wanted to make sure
the meeting is still on
for 2:30 tomorrow.

05:22.361 --> 05:24.133
Otherwise I gotta go
to that Chinese dentist.

05:24.201 --> 05:25.372
Get it? 2:30?

05:25.439 --> 05:26.879
(laughs)

05:26.947 --> 05:29.690
You son of a bitch, I had
a mouth full of coffee.

05:29.759 --> 05:32.169
God, you are funny,
and that is real!

05:32.237 --> 05:34.179
Okay, Peter,
Lois did great.

05:34.247 --> 05:36.724
You only need one point
to win the $5,000.

05:36.793 --> 05:37.930
20 seconds.

05:37.998 --> 05:39.602
Name something
you sit in.

05:39.671 --> 05:40.941
Chair.
(buzzer)

05:41.009 --> 05:42.715
Try again.
Big chair.

05:42.783 --> 05:44.320
(buzzer)
No, that's
the same thing.

05:44.388 --> 05:45.893
Try again.
High chair.

05:45.960 --> 05:47.899
That's still a chair.

05:47.967 --> 05:49.840
Chair.
Say something
other than "chair."

05:49.907 --> 05:51.076
What if I can't think
anything?

05:51.144 --> 05:52.748
You can pass.
How do I pass?

05:52.816 --> 05:53.919
Just say it.
Say what?

05:53.987 --> 05:55.558
Say "pass."

05:55.626 --> 05:56.764
Chair.
(buzzer)

05:56.832 --> 05:58.436
Oh, I'm sorry.
Your time is up,

05:58.505 --> 06:00.042
and you didn't score
enough points.

06:00.110 --> 06:01.247
But thank you
for playing.

06:01.316 --> 06:03.087
Whoa, what, that's it?
We lose?

06:03.156 --> 06:05.430
I'm afraid so, but we enjoyed
having you here.

06:05.498 --> 06:08.442
You son of a bitch,
what about my cave in the yard?

06:08.510 --> 06:10.115
What about my cave
in the yard?!

06:10.183 --> 06:11.554
Get your hands off me.

06:11.621 --> 06:13.629
I served
in the fictitious military.

06:15.303 --> 06:18.313
Peter! Oh, my God,
are you all right?

06:19.318 --> 06:20.454
What happened?

06:20.522 --> 06:22.160
Where am I?

06:22.228 --> 06:24.201
Who are you?
I'm Lois.

06:24.270 --> 06:26.208
Lois who?

06:26.277 --> 06:27.715
Who the hell am I?

06:27.783 --> 06:29.256
Uh-oh.

06:51.686 --> 06:53.828
Mrs. Griffin, I'm afraid
your husband has amnesia.

06:54.196 --> 06:56.471
Oh, my God,
is it permanent?

06:56.538 --> 06:57.977
Well, there's no telling
for sure.

06:58.045 --> 06:59.985
His memory could return
in days, weeks,

07:00.053 --> 07:01.826
years, or never.

07:01.894 --> 07:03.197
Or weeks.

07:05.741 --> 07:08.686
Peter, I want you
to meet your family.

07:08.755 --> 07:10.995
You're... my family?

07:11.063 --> 07:12.199
That's right.

07:12.268 --> 07:13.703
These are
your children.

07:13.772 --> 07:15.208
Dad, I'm Chris.

07:15.276 --> 07:16.612
I-I'm your son.

07:16.680 --> 07:18.217
Never seen you before
in my life.

07:18.286 --> 07:21.293
Wow, then I must
be invisible!

07:22.565 --> 07:25.510
Hey, everybody, I'm invisible!

07:25.577 --> 07:27.517
HERBERT:
Oh, no, you're not!

07:27.584 --> 07:28.921
Hot diggity!

07:29.960 --> 07:31.297
This is Meg,
your daughter.

07:31.365 --> 07:32.501
D'oh!

07:32.569 --> 07:34.309
No, Peter, that's not
your catchphrase.

07:34.377 --> 07:35.347
Oh.

07:35.414 --> 07:37.824
Sorry, I just don't
remember anything.

07:37.891 --> 07:40.535
Dad, this is your baby
and your dog.

07:40.603 --> 07:41.873
Ooh, he doesn't
remember us.

07:41.941 --> 07:43.946
It's an opportunity to come up
with our own names.

07:44.014 --> 07:45.618
I'm Tomax
and this is Xamot.

07:45.686 --> 07:48.128
We're twins who can feel
eachther's pain.

07:48.196 --> 07:49.466
Ow!
No, Brian,

07:49.534 --> 07:50.806
I'm supposed
to say "ow!"

07:50.874 --> 07:52.711
You ruin everything!

07:52.780 --> 07:53.784
Ow.

07:56.394 --> 07:58.601
All right, Peter, we're going
to try to jog your memory

07:58.668 --> 08:00.542
with some old videotapes
of the family.

08:00.609 --> 08:02.147
Boy, you got
a lot of tapes here.

08:02.214 --> 08:04.489
I kinda want to watch
some of these instead.

08:04.556 --> 08:06.095
<i>Pretty Woman?
What's that?</i>

08:06.162 --> 08:07.567
It's just a movie
from the '80s.

08:07.635 --> 08:09.408
Oh, my God, we gotta watch this.

08:09.476 --> 08:10.745
Look what they're
saying about it.

08:10.814 --> 08:13.388
"As funny as it is touching!
Gene Shalit."

08:13.456 --> 08:16.230
"I stood up and cheered,
'Go, Julia, go!'

08:16.299 --> 08:17.736
Joel Siegel."

08:17.805 --> 08:20.747
"This movie made me laugh
so hard I had mild headaches.

08:20.816 --> 08:23.592
"So I went to the doctor
and got myself checked out.

08:23.660 --> 08:26.269
I'm currently awaiting results.
Gene Siskel."

08:26.337 --> 08:28.643
Everyone seems to love this.
We gotta watch it!

08:28.711 --> 08:30.350
We'll watch it
later, Peter.

08:30.418 --> 08:32.859
I want to show you one
of the most special times

08:32.927 --> 08:36.674
of your life and mine:
our honeymoon.

08:44.742 --> 08:46.681
LOIS:
I think you've had enough,
Peter.

08:46.749 --> 08:48.119
(slurring):
Oh, you don't know...

08:48.187 --> 08:51.197
Get away. I-I know my
body better than you!

08:52.905 --> 08:54.677
Is that... us?

08:54.745 --> 08:55.947
Yes, Peter.

08:56.015 --> 08:57.287
You were so handsome

08:57.354 --> 09:00.030
and it was such
a wonderful week.

09:00.098 --> 09:03.040
Hey, buddy, I think
that girl likes me.

09:03.109 --> 09:04.815
Of course she does.
She's your wife.

09:04.882 --> 09:06.086
Do you like her?

09:06.154 --> 09:08.094
I don't know.

09:08.161 --> 09:10.636
(squeals, laughs)

09:10.704 --> 09:12.008
(sighs)

09:12.075 --> 09:14.082
You know, this isn't going
to be easy, you guys.

09:14.149 --> 09:15.789
We're going to have
to re-teach your father

09:15.857 --> 09:17.363
everything
he's forgotten.

09:17.430 --> 09:19.171
Hey, have you heard
this awesome new song?

09:19.239 --> 09:20.175
No!

09:20.243 --> 09:21.547
♪ A well, a bird,
bird, bird ♪

09:21.615 --> 09:22.652
♪ B-bird's the word ♪

09:22.720 --> 09:23.989
♪ A well, a bird,
bird, bird ♪

09:24.057 --> 09:25.462
♪ B-bird's the word,
a well, a...♪

09:28.006 --> 09:29.945
This is called
a telephone, Peter.

09:30.013 --> 09:32.690
You use it to talk to people
who aren't in the house.

09:32.759 --> 09:33.897
There are others?

09:33.966 --> 09:36.811
Yes, there are over six billion
people in the world.

09:36.879 --> 09:38.016
Here, I'll show you.

09:38.084 --> 09:39.891
We'll call my parents.

09:39.959 --> 09:41.296
CARTER:
Hello?

09:41.365 --> 09:42.567
Hello.

09:42.635 --> 09:44.006
Who's this?
Who's this?

09:44.074 --> 09:45.312
Carter. Who's this?

09:45.379 --> 09:47.150
I don't know.

09:47.218 --> 09:49.157
Do you have my OxyContin?
What?

09:49.225 --> 09:51.165
Are you the guy?
I'm a guy.

09:51.232 --> 09:52.670
I want my drugs.

09:52.739 --> 09:54.008
What are drugs?

09:54.076 --> 09:56.618
I don't think this is the call
I was expecting.

09:56.686 --> 09:57.689
(hangs up)

10:00.198 --> 10:02.640
Now, Peter, this is
your silverware.

10:02.708 --> 10:04.246
You see, this
is your fork.

10:04.315 --> 10:05.484
And this is a knife.

10:05.551 --> 10:07.258
That's not a knife.

10:07.326 --> 10:08.965
That's a knife.

10:09.032 --> 10:10.637
This is also a knife.

10:10.705 --> 10:11.943
Oh.

10:12.011 --> 10:13.985
Well, I'll be
on m' way.

10:14.052 --> 10:16.996
I want to see more of him,
and then suddenly none of him.

10:17.064 --> 10:18.569
Forever.

10:18.637 --> 10:20.643
(tires squealing, screeching)

10:23.389 --> 10:24.961
All right, you know what?

10:25.029 --> 10:26.164
This is not working.

10:26.232 --> 10:27.403
If you're going
to learn to drive,

10:27.470 --> 10:29.040
you're going to have
to practice first.

10:29.108 --> 10:31.716
Here, play "Grand Theft
Auto" for eight hours,

10:31.785 --> 10:34.595
and then we'll give
it another try.

10:43.932 --> 10:44.934
(tires squealing)

10:48.047 --> 10:49.686
So, you guys are
my best friends,

10:49.755 --> 10:51.393
and this is where
we hang out?

10:51.460 --> 10:52.562
That's right.

10:52.630 --> 10:54.035
I'm Quagmire,
and this is Joe.

10:54.103 --> 10:55.441
So, what do we do here?

10:55.508 --> 10:57.548
Well, we usually come here,
you buy us drinks

10:57.616 --> 10:59.421
and tell us what Loi''
nipples look like,

10:59.489 --> 11:00.591
like you
always do.

11:00.660 --> 11:01.763
Giggity-giggity.

11:01.830 --> 11:03.870
Yeah, but first,
you usually go over there

11:03.938 --> 11:06.211
and pull down
that blonde waitress's top.

11:07.618 --> 11:08.720
(woman screams)

11:08.789 --> 11:09.892
(loud slap)

11:09.959 --> 11:12.067
She screamed,
so I had to slap her.

11:16.856 --> 11:18.396
Oh, boy, oh, boy, oh, boy.

11:18.464 --> 11:20.405
Get nude. Get nude.
Please get nude.

11:20.473 --> 11:21.811
Please get nude.

11:21.879 --> 11:23.853
Peter, you don't
have to spy on me.

11:23.920 --> 11:25.156
You're my husband.

11:25.225 --> 11:26.696
Come on in.

11:26.765 --> 11:28.102
Oh, boy, no fooling?

11:28.170 --> 11:29.274
Oh, boy!

11:29.342 --> 11:30.445
Wait a minute.

11:30.512 --> 11:31.783
Something's happening
in my pants.

11:31.851 --> 11:33.088
In the front this time.

11:33.156 --> 11:34.558
That's all
right, Peter.

11:34.626 --> 11:36.633
It just means
you're excited.

11:36.701 --> 11:38.474
That's the way
it's supposed to be

11:38.541 --> 11:40.246
between a husband
and wife.

11:40.315 --> 11:42.256
It means you want
to make love.

11:42.325 --> 11:45.067
But I forget how
to make love.

11:45.135 --> 11:46.373
Shh, shh, shh, shh.

11:46.440 --> 11:47.811
That's okay.

11:47.880 --> 11:49.148
I'll show you.

11:49.216 --> 11:50.786
Just follow my lead.

11:52.058 --> 11:57.109
♪ It feels like the first time ♪

11:57.177 --> 12:00.555
♪ It feels like
the very first time... ♪

12:16.786 --> 12:18.859
(moaning)

12:18.927 --> 12:22.039
Wow! That was what
they call sex?

12:22.106 --> 12:23.845
Yes, it was, Peter.

12:23.913 --> 12:25.183
Can we do it again?

12:25.252 --> 12:26.757
Huh? Huh? Can we?

12:26.825 --> 12:28.029
Wow!

12:28.096 --> 12:30.806
You're as excited as a porcupine
meeting a pineapple.

12:32.313 --> 12:34.856
Hey, good-looking,
where have you been all my life?

12:34.924 --> 12:36.932
(laughs)

12:41.986 --> 12:44.494
Morning, nice people who
I still don't know your names

12:44.563 --> 12:46.068
and who mean nothing to me.

12:46.135 --> 12:48.478
Well, I certainly hope
that doesn't apply to me,

12:48.546 --> 12:50.653
especially after
last night.

12:50.720 --> 12:52.527
You got a point
there, hot stuff.

12:52.595 --> 12:54.166
And if sex with the rest of you

12:54.234 --> 12:56.040
is half as good
as it was with her,

12:56.108 --> 12:58.616
then I think we're all gonna
get along just fine.

12:58.684 --> 12:59.956
Yay!

13:00.023 --> 13:02.731
Well, no, no, Peter, you can't
have sex with the kids.

13:02.800 --> 13:05.709
<i>Well, I wish you'd told him that
before he lost his memory.</i>

13:05.778 --> 13:06.881
(gasps)

13:06.949 --> 13:08.085
It was a joke!

13:08.153 --> 13:09.757
I was just
making a joke.

13:09.825 --> 13:11.128
That's your
sense of humor?

13:11.196 --> 13:13.167
I was just
kidding. God!

13:13.234 --> 13:14.436
Meg, that's awful.

13:14.504 --> 13:16.711
Geez, you open your mouth
for a joke once,

13:16.779 --> 13:18.451
and that's what
you come up with?

13:18.519 --> 13:19.621
That's messed
up, Meg.

13:19.688 --> 13:21.060
I was just trying to be funny.

13:21.128 --> 13:23.134
That wasn't funny.
That was just dark.

13:23.201 --> 13:24.638
<i>Yeah, that's your father.</i>

13:24.706 --> 13:25.810
Oh, get out, Meg!

13:25.878 --> 13:26.980
Get out of the kitchen!

13:27.048 --> 13:29.122
Go on! Get out!
Out! Out! Out!

13:29.189 --> 13:30.829
Out of the kitchen! Go on!

13:30.896 --> 13:32.134
Get out of here!

13:32.201 --> 13:33.773
(laughs)

13:36.517 --> 13:38.791
Oh, Peter,
there you are.

13:38.859 --> 13:40.363
I've been waiting.

13:40.431 --> 13:42.103
You ready
to have sex?

13:42.171 --> 13:43.275
You bet.

13:43.342 --> 13:45.148
Move over
so Tiffany and I have room.

13:45.216 --> 13:46.554
What?! Who the
hell is she?

13:46.621 --> 13:48.629
She's the woman
I'm gonna have sex with tonight.

13:48.696 --> 13:50.503
Oh, and don't worry
about getting me pregnant.

13:50.571 --> 13:51.674
I'm already pregnant.

13:51.742 --> 13:53.382
Peter, what's the
matter with you?

13:53.449 --> 13:55.590
You can't just have sex
with some random woman.

13:55.658 --> 13:57.162
Why the hell not?

13:57.230 --> 13:58.335
Because we're married.

13:58.403 --> 13:59.505
Well, I'm sorry,

13:59.573 --> 14:00.978
but I don't remember
marrying anybody.

14:01.046 --> 14:03.890
Why the hell would I commit
to having sex with one person

14:03.958 --> 14:05.329
for the rest of my life?

14:05.396 --> 14:06.968
Because we love
each other.

14:07.036 --> 14:09.176
That's part of
being a family.

14:09.244 --> 14:11.586
It means being
responsible and faithful.

14:11.654 --> 14:13.259
Well, that doesn't sound
very fun.

14:13.327 --> 14:15.165
Well, if that's how you feel,

14:15.233 --> 14:17.707
then-then we no longer
have a family.

14:17.776 --> 14:19.180
Boy, I'm glad you said it.

14:19.248 --> 14:21.656
But this is my house,
and I'm not going anywhere.

14:21.724 --> 14:22.894
You don't have to.

14:22.962 --> 14:25.571
I'm leaving, and I'm
taking the kids with me.

14:26.979 --> 14:28.585
That's a beautiful necklace
you're wearing, Tiffany.

14:28.652 --> 14:30.086
Thank you.

14:30.155 --> 14:33.062
<i>Is that what you do with your
Saved By the Bell money?</i>

14:40.304 --> 14:43.150
Mom, I don't want to live
in a tiny, gross apartment.

14:43.218 --> 14:45.763
Well, I'm sorry, honey,
but we don't have a choice.

14:45.831 --> 14:47.270
Your father doesn't
remember his life,

14:47.337 --> 14:50.012
and he doesn't want us
to be a part of it,

14:50.080 --> 14:51.718
so we've just got
to move on.

14:51.787 --> 14:52.889
Oh, this is disgusting.

14:52.958 --> 14:54.228
I shouldn't be here.

14:54.296 --> 14:56.135
A baby doesn't belong
in the inner city

14:56.203 --> 14:58.243
any more than a baby
belongs on a plane.

14:58.312 --> 14:59.448
(crying)

14:59.516 --> 15:01.055
Shh. It's gonna be okay.

15:01.122 --> 15:02.660
Gonna be okay.

15:02.728 --> 15:05.471
<i>WOMAN (over P.A.):
Our in-flight movie this evening
is Hancock.</i>

15:05.539 --> 15:07.511
Waa! Waa!

15:07.579 --> 15:11.225
Waa! Waa!

15:11.294 --> 15:13.268
(rock music plays loudly)

15:19.492 --> 15:21.127
Peter, what the hell
is all this?

15:21.195 --> 15:22.300
Well, I'm a bachelor,

15:22.367 --> 15:24.173
so I invited a bunch
of people over,

15:24.241 --> 15:26.047
and now I'm waiting
for them to leave.

15:26.115 --> 15:27.219
That's what bachelors do.

15:27.288 --> 15:28.624
Peter, I'm interested
in the redhead

15:28.692 --> 15:30.497
with the wooden arms
and legs over there.

15:30.565 --> 15:31.902
You think you
could introduce me?

15:31.970 --> 15:33.775
That's a table,
Seamus.
Don't point at her.

15:33.843 --> 15:34.945
Don't point.
She's looking.

15:35.013 --> 15:36.685
Oh, great. Now
I got to go in.

15:36.754 --> 15:37.856
Hey, I'm Seamus.

15:37.924 --> 15:39.596
Peter, you left your family
for this?

15:39.663 --> 15:41.704
Look, I don't know
what I was doing before,

15:41.772 --> 15:44.047
but this is the way
man was meant to live.

15:44.115 --> 15:45.286
I just know it.

15:45.354 --> 15:46.457
Check it out.

15:46.525 --> 15:48.398
(moaning)

15:48.465 --> 15:49.968
Don't you miss your family?

15:50.036 --> 15:51.405
What, that lady
and those kids?

15:51.473 --> 15:53.580
I don't even remember 'em.
How could I miss them?

15:53.648 --> 15:55.186
I almost don't want
to ask you out

15:55.255 --> 15:56.592
because I know
you're gonna say no.

15:56.660 --> 15:57.765
You want to go out?

15:57.833 --> 15:59.004
No? Okay.

16:03.052 --> 16:05.660
<i>(to Jaws theme):
♪ Giggity ♪</i>

16:06.732 --> 16:08.907
♪ Giggity ♪

16:10.379 --> 16:11.950
♪ Gi-gi, gi-gi,
gi-gi, gi-gi ♪

16:12.018 --> 16:13.958
♪ Gi-gi, gi-gi,
gi-gi, gi-gi, gi-gi ♪

16:14.026 --> 16:14.962
♪ Gi-gi, gi-gi ♪

16:15.029 --> 16:16.301
♪ Gi-gi, gi-gi, gi-gi ♪

16:16.369 --> 16:19.145
♪ Gi-gi, gi-gi, gi-gi,
giggity! ♪

16:19.212 --> 16:20.886
Lois! Oh,
my gosh. Hi!

16:20.954 --> 16:22.056
Oh, hi, Quagmire.

16:22.124 --> 16:23.227
What a surprise.

16:23.295 --> 16:24.465
I know, right?

16:24.533 --> 16:26.807
Gosh, you know, I was just
picking up a couple hams

16:26.874 --> 16:29.318
to take down to the shelter,
and here I run into you,

16:29.386 --> 16:30.956
buying food to make
dinner for your husband.

16:31.024 --> 16:33.300
No, actually, Glenn,
maybe you haven't heard,

16:33.367 --> 16:36.076
but, uh, Peter and I
aren't together anymore.

16:36.143 --> 16:38.116
What?! Why?!

16:38.184 --> 16:39.389
Oh, it's a long story.

16:39.457 --> 16:41.229
You don't want to hear about it.

16:41.297 --> 16:42.399
Oh, shut your face.

16:42.468 --> 16:43.671
<i>I want to hear
all about it.</i>

16:43.739 --> 16:45.947
But listen, you know, I got
all this shopping to do,

16:46.014 --> 16:47.585
so you want to stop by
tomorrow night?

16:47.653 --> 16:48.858
I'll just whip
something up.

16:48.925 --> 16:50.062
Well, sure.

16:50.129 --> 16:52.136
You know,
that sounds nice, Glenn.

16:53.342 --> 16:55.784
Holy smokes,
this is a sure thing.

16:55.852 --> 16:57.792
Like the end
of a Mexican wedding.

16:57.859 --> 16:59.095
(applause)

16:59.163 --> 17:01.170
(cheering)

17:07.397 --> 17:08.733
Aw, crap, we're out of milk.

17:08.802 --> 17:11.345
I'm gonna run next door
to the airport and get some.

17:11.414 --> 17:13.822
Hey, when you're over there,
can you get some rodent traps?

17:13.890 --> 17:16.029
We got a giant mutant rat
living under the sink.

17:16.098 --> 17:18.037
I'm just gonna hide
under the sink

17:18.105 --> 17:19.543
till y'all go to sleep.

17:19.611 --> 17:22.052
Then I'm gonna come out
and make my poops in your Kix.

17:22.120 --> 17:23.458
Hey, Stewie,
is Lois back yet?

17:23.525 --> 17:25.599
I've been trying
to get a hold of her.

17:25.666 --> 17:27.005
She went to Quagmire's
for dinner.

17:27.072 --> 17:28.110
What?!

17:31.892 --> 17:33.865
Oh, that was a
delicious dinner, Glenn.

17:33.933 --> 17:35.505
I didn't know
you could cook.

17:35.573 --> 17:38.281
Well, when a fella's been alone
as long as I have,

17:38.349 --> 17:40.021
he learns
to take care of himself.

17:40.088 --> 17:41.895
Well, you're a
very sweet friend,

17:41.963 --> 17:44.169
and you're so good to
listen to my troubles.

17:44.236 --> 17:46.042
Oh, I could listen
for hours, Lois.

17:46.109 --> 17:47.682
Phew! Boy, you know,

17:47.749 --> 17:51.162
I don't know how a half a glass
of wine got me so lightheaded.

17:51.230 --> 17:52.534
I better lie down.

17:52.601 --> 17:54.376
You want me to
help you upstairs?

17:54.444 --> 17:56.452
Oh, my God,
you are a saint!

17:59.431 --> 18:01.973
No, I-I think I can make it
from here. I-I...

18:02.041 --> 18:03.713
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

18:03.781 --> 18:06.154
(both laughing)

18:06.222 --> 18:07.560
Whoops!

18:07.628 --> 18:09.534
Professor Klutz,
the doctor is in.

18:09.601 --> 18:10.839
(laughs)

18:10.907 --> 18:12.513
Oh, where is
this heading?

18:14.489 --> 18:16.328
Oh, hiya, Brian.

18:16.396 --> 18:17.533
All right, Peter,
now I know

18:17.601 --> 18:18.871
your head is still
a blank slate,

18:18.939 --> 18:20.846
but you got to listen
to me when I say...

18:20.913 --> 18:22.518
Wait. Did you just
call me Brian?

18:22.586 --> 18:23.688
Oh, yeah.

18:23.757 --> 18:25.194
You've got
your memory back?
Uh-huh.

18:25.262 --> 18:27.669
Happened yesterday on my way
back from the grocery store.

18:27.737 --> 18:29.444
Hi, Peter.

18:31.921 --> 18:34.468
Hey, you just snubbed me
in front of my own house.

18:34.536 --> 18:36.108
I thought we'd come
to an understanding.

18:36.175 --> 18:39.085
Look, fella, I don't know
who you are and I don't want to,

18:39.153 --> 18:41.327
so why don't you just go back
to your crabgrass?

18:41.396 --> 18:43.770
This happens to be
fresh Marathon Sod!

18:44.942 --> 18:47.551
Oh, man, I just got
my memory back.

18:47.618 --> 18:50.361
And as I recall,
I don't really care for you!

18:51.466 --> 18:53.005
Wait a minute.
Who are you?

18:53.072 --> 18:54.376
Hey, I know you!

18:54.444 --> 18:55.814
What's your beef, stranger?

18:55.882 --> 18:58.256
Well, if it isn't
my old nemesis!

18:58.324 --> 19:00.766
I was just lucky he had
an odd number of objects.

19:00.834 --> 19:02.338
Why the hell
didn't you tell anybody?

19:02.406 --> 19:04.379
Well, I figured I could
enjoy the bachelor life

19:04.447 --> 19:06.453
for a few more days
before getting Lois back.

19:06.521 --> 19:08.327
Well, you may have waited
too long already.

19:08.394 --> 19:09.865
Lois is on a date
with Quagmire,

19:09.933 --> 19:11.806
and you've got to stop her
before something happens.

19:11.874 --> 19:13.646
What?! Oh, my God! Where is she?

19:13.714 --> 19:15.117
She's next door at his house.

19:15.185 --> 19:16.623
And you better get there quick,

19:16.691 --> 19:18.298
because with Quagmire,
sex is inevitable.

19:18.365 --> 19:20.072
Like a fat guy ordering dessert

19:20.140 --> 19:21.745
when everyone else wants
to leave.

19:21.814 --> 19:24.120
So, does anyone
want dessert?

19:24.188 --> 19:25.660
Ah, I couldn't
eat another bite.

19:25.727 --> 19:27.935
No. I got to get home
for the sitter.

19:28.002 --> 19:29.105
I'll have
the soufflГѓВ©.

19:29.173 --> 19:30.277
That takes
45 minutes.

19:30.345 --> 19:31.516
That's okay.

19:35.300 --> 19:36.973
Oh, I can't believe
we're doing this,

19:37.041 --> 19:39.515
but I got to say,
it feels kind of right.

19:39.583 --> 19:41.289
I know, it's so
weird, right?

19:41.357 --> 19:43.430
I mean, it's... I mean,
it's, like, fast.

19:43.497 --> 19:46.540
I mean, it's fast, but it feels,
like, okay, you know?

19:46.608 --> 19:48.181
I mean, like,
isn't that crazy?

19:48.249 --> 19:50.559
It's like this adventure
that we're having together.

19:50.627 --> 19:53.102
I know. That's exactly
how I feel.

19:53.171 --> 19:55.279
I mean, it's a little strange,

19:55.346 --> 19:57.453
but if Peter's never
coming back to me,

19:57.520 --> 19:59.025
it's at least nice to know

19:59.093 --> 20:01.166
I'm in the arms
of a trusted friend.

20:01.234 --> 20:04.345
You... You trust me?

20:05.852 --> 20:07.055
Uh-oh.

20:07.123 --> 20:08.461
Wha...? Is something wrong?

20:08.528 --> 20:09.833
I-I-I don't know.

20:09.900 --> 20:12.277
I'll be right back.

20:12.344 --> 20:14.016
(rhythmic whooshing)

20:14.084 --> 20:15.219
Damn it!

20:15.288 --> 20:16.893
Lois!

20:16.961 --> 20:18.064
Peter?!

20:18.131 --> 20:19.468
What-What are you doing here?

20:19.536 --> 20:21.744
I got my memory back,
and I love you, Lois.

20:21.813 --> 20:23.351
I want you and the kids back.

20:23.419 --> 20:24.721
I want our old life back.

20:24.790 --> 20:25.894
(Lois laughs)

20:25.962 --> 20:27.198
I don't believe it!

20:27.267 --> 20:28.668
Sweetheart, it's you!

20:28.736 --> 20:29.906
You're back!

20:29.975 --> 20:31.312
QUAGMIRE:
Oh! Damn it!

20:31.379 --> 20:33.652
I'm back, Lois,
and I'm sorry.

20:33.720 --> 20:36.329
I treated you so badly,
but I hope you know

20:36.397 --> 20:38.571
it-it was only because
I wasn't myself.

20:38.639 --> 20:40.412
I didn't just
lose my memory.

20:40.480 --> 20:41.581
I lost my mind.

20:41.649 --> 20:42.754
Clear!

20:42.821 --> 20:44.024
(electrical buzzing)

20:44.092 --> 20:45.195
Damn it!

20:45.263 --> 20:46.903
Oh, my God, Peter,
I don't care!

20:46.970 --> 20:48.073
I don't care.

20:48.141 --> 20:49.781
I'm just overjoyed
to have you back!

20:49.849 --> 20:50.985
Let's go home!

20:51.053 --> 20:53.026
(electrical buzzing)

20:53.094 --> 20:54.432
QUAGMIRE:
Damn it!

20:54.500 --> 20:55.737
(buzzing)
Damn it.

20:55.738 --> 21:56.738
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru